ng so how  did Sally end up in the lead and also  the rest of the sketch terrific ensemble  and some of them in very small parts but  had it had it had come together  well max Greenfield attached himself to  it very early on max is a friend of mine  I had worked with him on another movie  and he was the first person on board  when we when we offered it to say we we  have like a window to make the movie  which was the summer of 2014 I think and  so I was very afraid to send the script  to Sally because I didn't think she  would do it and and I didn't want I was  afraid that we would take forever  because she's a big huge giant movie  star and even though she's the only  person we would have ever wanted to play  the role it was it was kind of scary but  everyone was like we just let's just  take a chance you know and and she  obviously wanted to do the movie and  then once you have Sally Field it's kind  of easy to get those other actors  I mean you to be able to say to all the  other actors that are in the movie this  movie is financed and Sally Field was  playing the lead it piques their  interest and so it what you know it was  a that at that point it was about you  know availability and the actors  obviously needing to respond to the  material but that helps you get in the  door really easily so we were just able  to just look at actors that we loved and  say hey this person would be amazing  Tyne Daly or Steven route or you know  Wendy mclendon-covey or all these  amazing great funny dramatic actors that  we got for the movie we just made them  offers and and and so that's kind of how  it happened so the production three  weeks three and a half right now we did  three weeks in LA and three days in New  York how does that what does that feel  like when you're in the middle of it  it was a very business it was a fun set  but it was not a loose set and that was  a function of that we were obviously  under incredible time constraints but  also Sally Field set a tone 