urie are you want to  sir so I mean for me a lot of what the  film is about is visibility and how in  our culture older women sort of become  invisible and Doris would not go down  without a fight you know and when sort  of that's to me what you know but I  wanted to look at with this film and and  so I'm and I I'm really pleased with the  responses people seem to appreciate it  on both the comedic level and a dramatic  one and so yeah I couldn't be happier  and and for me I would say that there's  a theme for the movie it's that it's  never too late to start something and  it's possible to change and in terms of  the response I mean I'm happy extremely  gratified that Sally Fields performance  is being recognized that's so that's  really all I care about  you know and it's I mean it's amazing  it's amazing to to to see people I don't  I'm you know it's amazing to go to a  movie theater and be like there's people  here in the movie theater just because  they want to see the movie not because  they're my friends or my family and I  had to beg them to come see it you know  like it's a crazy feeling to be like  they're just here because they want to  see the movie and and so as the person  who knows the people making the movie  that's like you can't that's that is the  greatest feeling ever is to know that  like they're there really because they  just want to be there they want to see  Sally Field playing this role and it's  great thank you very much thank you for  coming thanks for coming

